==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Master of Selection Clawvin''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Master of Selection Clawvin is a midrange tank and crowd-controller hybrid that targets [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]]/[[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]]/[[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]]. He has a very respectable 837,000 effective HP against targets at Lv.50, alongside a [[Weaken]] and [[Curse]] that retain a 60% uptime on average. He handily shuts down a majority of melee pushers within his targets, such as [[Angelic Gory]], [[Scissoroo]], or [[Doctor K.O.]], while controlling them from a relatively safe distance. This isn't mentioning the utility Curse provides against Aliens specifically, as most tend to carry disruptive abilities that he can completely bypass. He does very well against [[I.M. Phace]]'s Freeze, disables [[Calamary]]'s Weaken with his high pierce, and completely trivializes the Warp from enemies like [[Commander Ostromeda]], [[Mesocosmocyclone]], [[Star Peng]], among others because of his [[Immune to Warp|immunity]].

He also has [[Sage Slayer]], which gives him ridiculously powerful stat boosts that specifically improves matchups against two enemies in particular: [[Techn-Old Hyena]] and Doctor K.O. While the former cannot be Cursed, he can still be Weakened, upping Clawvin's effective HP to a gargantuan 3,348,000 (2,678,400 on average, accounting for the uptime of Weaken). It becomes much easier to burst Techn-Old Hyena down with units such as [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] or [[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:NX]]. The same applies to Doctor K.O., proving that these enemies must evolve to keep up with Clawvin.

However, this isn't to say that he doesn't have any problems in practice. For one, this tortoise is slow and steady but won't be winning any race, which means most enemies that outrange him are going to get the first strike on him. And, of course, he can't tank [[Poultrio]] or [[Angelic Sleipnir]] all too well if he's struggling to reach them and getting constantly interrupted. Furthermore, his recharge time is quite long, and while not exactly fragile, his base HP against non-targets means you have to ensure he doesn't catch too many strays. Thankfully, his [[Conjure]] acts as an emergency escape button with [[Knockback]] if they are ever put in grave danger.

Master of Selection Clawvin is a good support/tank all in all, but should be used intelligently to get the most value out of him. Even the cats can't outrun natural selection, after all.

